# AI flashcard generation

AI features in this app call OpenAI through the Vercel AI SDK package `ai`.
Do not add `@ai-sdk/openai`, the OpenAI SDK, or another model provider, and do
not call the OpenAI HTTP API directly. The only model string is
`"openai/gpt-6-astra"`.

The only AI feature is flashcard generation. It creates cards for a deck the
signed-in user owns. Each generated card has a `front` and a `back`, matching
the columns on `cards` in [src/db/schema.ts](mdc:src/db/schema.ts).

## Where the call runs

`generateText` runs only inside a Server Action, after Zod `safeParse` and the
`userId` check, and only when `has({ feature: "ai_flashcard_generation" })` is
true. Billing follows
[.cursor/rules/clerk-billing.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/clerk-billing.mdc). A
missing feature returns an error and does not write `cards`.

A page, Client Component, or Route Handler does not import `generateText` or
`Output`. The action receives a plain object (topic and the requested count).
It does not read `FormData`.

## Structured output

Generate the cards with `generateText` and `Output.array` from `ai`. Set
`minItems` and `maxItems` to the same requested count so the array length is
exactly that number. Each element is an object with `front` and `back` strings.
`output` is that array.

```ts
import { generateText, Output } from "ai"
import { z } from "zod"

const count = 10

const { output } = await generateText({
  model: "openai/gpt-6-astra",
  output: Output.array({
    element: z.object({
      front: z.string(),
      back: z.string(),
    }),
    minItems: count,
    maxItems: count,
  }),
  prompt: `Generate ${count} flashcards. Each card has a front and a back.`,
})
```

`count` is the validated number of cards the action was asked to create. Use
that same number for `minItems`, `maxItems`, and the prompt. Do not use
`Output.object` for this feature, and do not use `generateObject`.

## Saving the cards

After `output` is returned, insert each card through the helpers in
[src/db/queries/cards.ts](mdc:src/db/queries/cards.ts), as required by
[.cursor/rules/data-access.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/data-access.mdc). Pass the
`userId` from `auth()` and the deck id. Map `front` and `back` from each
element onto those helpers. Do not insert from the model call itself.
